# Architecture invariants

> These are properties that must remain true while implementation changes. Record the trade-off in
> an ADR when an invariant is created, narrowed, or replaced.

## Boundary invariants

- [A dependency, integration, or domain boundary that must remain explicit.]
- [A rule for isolating external-system or framework-specific behavior.]

## Data and compatibility invariants

- [A durability, ownership, versioning, or compatibility property.]
- [A rule for migration, deletion, or recovery of important state.]

## Reliability and safety invariants

- [A failure mode that must degrade safely.]
- [A limit on automated, irreversible, or externally visible behavior.]

## Explainability and change invariants

- [Information needed to explain a consequential output or decision.]
- [A rollback, approval, or versioning property for material changes.]

